## 🚀 Getting Started

### Prerequisites
* Python 3.10+
* Node.js v18+ (if running React frontend)
* Virtual environment tool (`venv` or `conda`)

### Installation & Setup

1. **Clone the repository:**
   ```bash
   git clone [https://github.com/your-username/rural-business-advisory-ai.git](https://github.com/your-username/rural-business-advisory-ai.git)
   cd rural-business-advisory-ai

Set up virtual environment:
python -m venv venv
source venv/bin/activate  # On Windows: venv\Scripts\activate

Install dependencies:
pip install -r requirements.txt

Configure Environment Variables:
Create a .env file in the root directory:
OPENAI_API_KEY=your_openai_api_key
BHASHINI_API_KEY=your_bhashini_translation_key
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@localhost:5432/rural_advisory_db

Run the Application:
uvicorn app.main:app --reload

Sample Input & Output Workflow
User Input Example
Location: Village Khed, District Pune, Maharashtra
Available Margin Capital: ₹1,00,000
Business Category: Dairy Farming & Milk Processing

Key Impact Goals
Risk Reduction: Lowers failure rate of newly funded rural micro-enterprises through data-backed business strategy.
Financial Clarity: Eliminates ambiguity by directly linking available cash to exact borrowing eligibility and repayment structures.
Grassroots Empowerment: Democratizes advisory tools for marginalized entrepreneurs in native regional languages.
